# {{DISPLAY_NAME}}

A ZetaForge plugin.

```bash
zeta dev        # build, install and run on every save
zeta build      # produce dist/{{NAME}}-1.0.0.zeta
zeta test       # unit tests, no device needed
zeta inspect dist/{{NAME}}-1.0.0.zeta
```

## Layout

| | |
|---|---|
| `zetaplugin.toml` | identity, permissions, settings, dependencies |
| `src/` | the Kotlin code |
| `test/` | JVM tests |
| `dist/` | the packaged `.zeta` |

Everything else — build files, the Gradle wrapper, dependency wiring — is
generated into `.zeta/` and can be deleted at any time.

## Distributing it

The `.zeta` in `dist/` is the whole plugin. Send it to anyone with ZetaForge
installed and they can import it — no store, no account, no signing.
